Lobium — register the //components/lobium_fp config-channel module in the build graph.

Wires the added first-party module (components/lobium_fp/, staged by lobium/build.sh) into Blink so the
navigator/UA-CH/screen/WebGL/... hooks can read lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current():
  - blink core (component("core")) deps += //components/lobium_fp:lobium_fp
  - blink core DEPS include-rule += +components/lobium_fp

Kept minimal, and in the //components first-party root rather than //third_party (which the license
scanner tools/licenses.py rejects for a directory lacking README.chromium/LICENSE, breaking the
is_official_build credits step). COMPILE-VERIFIED on Chromium 152.0.7928.0.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/BUILD.gn b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/BUILD.gn
index a4a53a9003..e5143277a2 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/BUILD.gn
@@ -410,6 +410,7 @@ component("core") {
     "//base",
     "//components/attribution_reporting",
     "//components/attribution_reporting:mojom_blink",
+    "//components/lobium_fp:lobium_fp",
     "//components/paint_preview/common",
     "//components/performance_manager/public/mojom:mojom_blink",
     "//components/shared_highlighting/core/common",
